ERROR REPORTS

Please send errors and suggestions to Frans Kaashoek and Robert Morris
(kaashoek,rtm@mit.edu). The main purpose of xv6 is as a teaching
operating system for MIT's 6.1810, so we are more interested in
simplifications and clarifications than new features.

BUILDING AND RUNNING XV6

You will need a RISC-V "newlib" tool chain from
https://github.com/riscv/riscv-gnu-toolchain, and qemu compiled for
riscv64-softmmu. Once they are installed, and in your shell
search path, you can run "make qemu".

# Page Tables

## Question 1

### For every page table entry in the print_pgtbl output, explain what it logically contains and what its permission bits are. Figure 3.4 in the xv6 book might be helpful, although note that the figure might have a slightly different set of pages than process that's being inspected here.

#### Raw Data

<p>
Quick Notes:
1. pa I think stands for physical address
</p>

1.  va 0x0 pte 0x21FC885B pa 0x87F22000 perm 0x5B

<p> 
Contains: Root of the tree, a 4096-byte page table 
</p>
<p>
Permission bits: 0x5B = 0101 1011
Therefore contains accessed, user, executable, readable and valid
</p>

2.  va 0x1000 pte 0x21FC7C17 pa 0x87F1F000 perm 0x17

<p> 
Contains: The first "high-level" pte that is access by va 0x1000, which is stored in the kernel space
</p>
<p>
Permission bits: 0x17 = 0001 0111 = 
Therefore contains user, executable, readable and valid
</p>
3.  va 0x2000 pte 0x21FC7807 pa 0x87F1E000 perm 0x7
<p> 
Contains: The 2nd high level pte that is accessed via 0x2000 
</p>
<p>
Permission bits: 0000 0111
Therefore contains writable, readable and valid
</p>

4.  va 0x3000 pte 0x21FC74D7 pa 0x87F1D000 perm 0xD7
<p> 
Contains: A recently written file that is still "high level" page
</p>
<p>
Permission bits: 0xD7 = 1101 0111 = 
Therefore contains Dirty, Accessed, User, writable, readable and valid
</p>

5.  va 0x4000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p> 
Contains: Nothing, empty page 
</p>
<p>
Permission bits: no permissions 
</p>

6.  va 0x5000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p>same as 5. </p>

7.  va 0x6000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p>same as 5. </p>

8.  va 0x7000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p>same as 5. </p>

9.  va 0x8000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p>same as 5. </p>

10. va 0x9000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p>same as 5. </p>

11. va 0xFFFF6000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p> 
contains nothing
</p>
12. va 0xFFFF7000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p> 
contains nothing
</p>

13. va 0xFFFF8000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p> 
contains nothing
</p>

14. va 0xFFFF9000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p> 
contains nothing
</p>

15. va 0xFFFFA000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p> 
contains nothing
</p>

16. va 0xFFFFB000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p> 
contains nothing
</p>

17. va 0xFFFFC000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p> 
contains nothing
</p>

18. va 0xFFFFD000 pte 0x0 pa 0x0 perm 0x0
<p> 
contains nothing
</p>

19. va 0xFFFFE000 pte 0x21FD08C7 pa 0x87F42000 perm 0xC7
<p>
Contains: L2, L1 and partial L0 but not offset
</p>
<p>
permission: 0xC7 = 1100 0111 
Permission for dirty, accessed, writable, readable ,valid
</p>

20. va 0xFFFFF000 pte 0x2000184B pa 0x80006000 perm 0x4B
<p> </p>
